{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The righteous man.</b> These are the deeds of the shepherds: the righteous perish, and no one sets it upon his heart to say, why do the righteous perish and these wicked live? And behold, this is the prophet's interpretation: the righteous man is gathered before he sees the evil coming upon Israel and upon the holy city."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:53.794993525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}